## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design an OTCA-compliant data lineage and provenance service at PayPal and Netflix scale, with strict multi-tenant privacy requirements.

## Key Concepts

- **Tamper-evident ledger**: Hash-chain linked records ensure immutability and forensic integrity
- **Residency enforcement**: Region-scoped storage prevents cross-border data leakage
- **Cryptographic signing**: RSASSA-PSS or ECDSA signatures authenticate record origin
- **Policy engine**: OPA (Open Policy Agent) for fine-grained, cross-region access control
- **Write-once storage**: Object Lock or append-only databases guarantee audit trail integrity
- **Testing**: Replay attacks, backfill scenarios, fault injection, and region failover validation

## Code Example

```javascript
function signRecord(rec, privateKey) {
  const payload = JSON.stringify(rec);
  const encoder = new TextEncoder();
  return crypto.subtle.sign(
    { name: 'RSASSA-PSS', saltLength: 32 },
    privateKey,
    encoder.encode(payload)
  );
}

function verifyRecord(rec, signature, publicKey) {
  const payload = JSON.stringify(rec);
  const encoder = new TextEncoder();
  return crypto.subtle.verify(
    { name: 'RSASSA-PSS', saltLength: 32 },
    publicKey,
    signature,
    encoder.encode(payload)
  );
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes governance architecture across OTCA, focusing on immutability, auditability, regional residency, and rollback semantics in policy updates.

## Key Concepts
- Region residency and local sinks
- Versioned, immutable policy logs
- Global reconciler with audit trail
- Rollback and cross-region consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
function isNewVersion(current, incoming) {
  const toNum = s => (s||'0').split('.').map(n => parseInt(n,10));
  const [a,b,c] = toNum(current);
  const [x,y,z] = toNum(incoming);
  if (x !== a) return x > a;
  if (y !== b) return y > b;
  return (z||0) > (c||0);
}
```

